## 🎯 Code Quality & Best Practices

### ✅ SOLID Principles
- **S**ingle Responsibility: Each controller handles one resource
- **O**pen/Closed: Routes are extensible without modification
- **L**iskov Substitution: Middleware can be replaced
- **I**nterface Segregation: Controllers expose specific methods
- **D**ependency Inversion: Using abstraction layers

### ✅ Security
- ✅ Password hashing with bcrypt (10 rounds)
- ✅ JWT token validation
- ✅ Role-based access control
- ✅ CORS configuration
- ✅ Input validation and sanitization
- ✅ Environment variables for sensitive data

### ✅ Code Standards
- ✅ Comprehensive comments and documentation
- ✅ Consistent naming conventions
- ✅ Error handling throughout
- ✅ Proper HTTP status codes
- ✅ Responsive UI/UX
- ✅ Loading and error states

